// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// M3.9 -- populate the rest of the Felucca world.
//
// The shard owner asked for the whole world: "graveyards, destard, ice area,
// deceit etc". The dungeons were already placed in M3.8 (twelve classic ones
// survive after f_m39_prune_ml removed the Mondain's Legacy strays), and
// Vendors, Towns Life and Wild Life were placed in earlier milestones. What was
// still missing is everything below.
//
// EVERY SET HERE WAS AUDITED BEFORE BEING RUN. That ordering is the whole point:
// M3.8 ran an aggregate spawn function without reading it and placed eleven
// unrenderable ML spawners that had to be pruned afterwards. The audit resolved
// all 787 creature tokens in these sets through spawner_defs.scp to a CHARDEF
// and then to the file defining it, flagging anything from aos/se/ml/sa/hs/tol.
//
//   Graveyards   CLEAN, but replaced by f_m39_graveyards -- the stock function
//                puts a graveyard at "Haven", a TRAMMEL settlement whose
//                Felucca coordinates land on Ocllo island.
//   Outdoors     TWO ML creatures (changeling, plaguespawn) out of 445
//                spawners -- replaced by f_m39_outdoors, which drops those two
//                tokens and changes nothing else.
//   Sea Life     CLEAN. Dolphin, sea serpent, deep sea serpent, kraken,
//                sea horse, water elemental -- all classic.
//   Reagents     CLEAN. Item spawners for the eight ordinary reagents, which
//                also matters for M3.9's reagent-sourcing debt: with
//                ReagentsRequired=1 a mage must actually find these.
//   Lost Lands   CLEAN. T2A (1998) content -- Ophidians, Terathans, ostards,
//                Efreet. Comfortably inside the 2008-2010 window.
//
// NOT RUN, and deliberately so:
//   spawn_quest_npcs_felucca      327 ML Heartwood elves + a necromancer
//                                 trainer; the client cannot render elves
//   everything under trammel/     Revolution had no second facet
//   malas/ tokuno/ termur/        AoS / SE / SA
//   spawn_uoclassic               1,770 duplicates of the Nerun set
//
// RUN ONCE. f_create_spawner has no idempotency -- running this twice places a
// second full set of spawners on top of the first. Verify by counting
// i_worldgem_bit in the world save before and after, the same way the ML prune
// was verified, and not by trusting any number this function prints.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

[function f_m39_populate]
SRC.SYSMESSAGE @,,1 m39 populate: graveyards...
f_m39_graveyards
SRC.SYSMESSAGE @,,1 m39 populate: outdoors (445 spawners, this takes a moment)...
f_m39_outdoors
SRC.SYSMESSAGE @,,1 m39 populate: sea life...
spawn_sea_life_felucca
SRC.SYSMESSAGE @,,1 m39 populate: reagents...
spawn_reagents_felucca
SRC.SYSMESSAGE @,,1 m39 populate: lost lands...
spawn_lost_lands_felucca
SRC.SYSMESSAGE @,,1 m39 populate COMPLETE -- verify by spawner count in the world save
RETURN 1

[eof]
